.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
dist/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
*.nupkg
# Solution manifests (*.uipx) are source: keep them. Ignore only the build zips that
# `uip solution pack` writes (<Name>_<version>.zip in <Name>_out/ or the --output folder).
**/*_out/
**/*_[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.zip
**/.local/
# Coded-agent local runtime state (LangGraph checkpoint DB written by uip codedagent run) — never commit
**/__uipath/
# uipath Python SDK / coded app local state (uipath auth writes the access and refresh token to .uipath/.auth.json)
**/.uipath/
# Lab 9 audit exports contain actor emails
**/audit-export/*.csv
**/audit-export/**/*.json
# Maestro debug overwrites carry tenant and user ids; deploy configs and token files are per tenant
**/userProfile/
deploy-config*.json
*.token
# Lab 10: `uip solution resources refresh` regenerates resources/ (feed URLs, tenant ids and, before
# stripping, the signed ERP token)
lab10-maestro-bpmn/*/resources/
# Challenge (homework): `uip solution resources refresh` regenerates resources/ the same way as Lab 10
challenge-maestro-flow/*/resources/
# Lab 10 (Step 6): never commit solution build output, registry caches, tenant ids or secrets
lab10-maestro-bpmn/**/*.zip
lab10-maestro-bpmn/**/*.nupkg
lab10-maestro-bpmn/**/packages/
**/registry-evidence/
**/.registry-cache/
**/debug_overwrites.json
*.pfx
*.pem
*.signed-url
lab10-maestro-bpmn/**/*secret*
# Scaffold briefing files written by `uip solution init`; the reference leaves them out too
lab10-maestro-bpmn/*/AGENTS.md
lab10-maestro-bpmn/*/CLAUDE.md
